In article <1991May24.132304.31038@kuhub.cc.ukans.edu>, montulli@kuhub.cc.ukans.edu writes...
> I seem to have a small problem.  I installed nethack on our VAX 9000 system 
> running VMS 5.4-1 but there is a glitch.  After running INSTALL.COM Nethack
> runs fine, but if you logout and log back in again, it will not run.

     You should have edited [.include]vmsconf.h prior to compiling the
program.  That's where nethack.exe gets its idea of the location of the
playground, and also the user who's allowed to access debug mode.  The
value used by install.com should match what you used in vmsconf.h.

     If they didn't match, you can still fix things without rebuilding.
The logical name HACKDIR overrides the playground location at run time.
 |$ DEFINE HACKDIR disk:[dir.subdir]
   (fill in the proper device and directory above)
 |$ MCR HACKDIR:NETHACK -u"Conan-B" -dec  !play as Conan, using VT graphics
   (or perhaps SET DEFAULT HACKDIR followed by RUN NETHACK)

     The installation procedure defines HACKDIR as part of its operation.
That definition went away when you logged out.  You should probably insert
its definition into your login.com procedure, so that it's redefined every
time you log in.  Better yet, have your system manager setup a system-wide
definition.

